Rust API
========

Rustdoc is generated with
``cargo doc --no-deps --no-default-features`` for the selected Rust output.
The generated crate exposes primitive functions through the public ``profile``
module. This reference renders a profile-neutral union of the generated Rust
primitive APIs, so no concrete machine-profile Cargo feature is selected and
each primitive appears once. Concrete profile availability and implementation
state belong to the specialization reference. The opaque root ``Simd`` and
``Mask`` facade and the selected ``profile`` primitive module are the stable
TSL 1.x Rust surface. ``tsl_core`` and ``tsl_algorithm`` remain reachable
because generated signatures depend on them, but are intentionally hidden from
the stable index and their representations are not a stable ABI.

Normal crate builds select the best generated profile through compile-target
``cfg(target_feature)`` predicates and use the generated generic fallback when
no native profile matches. Cargo does not expose one feature per machine
profile. The optional ``runtime-dispatch`` feature is a separate ``std``-based
mode.

Unsuffixed lower-level calls do not sanitize their operands. UB-capable calls
are ``unsafe fn``; checked companions use slices or references where necessary
and return ``Result<_, PreconditionError>``. See
:doc:`checked_api_contract` for the shared two-path contract and residual
obligations.

Generated test helpers and physical ``tsl_<profile>`` module names are
implementation details and are hidden from the API index.

`Open the Rust API reference <rust/index.html>`_
